data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

In .NET 10, the Cosmos DB provider allowed you to opt into sync-over-async behavior (e.g., via `CosmosOptionsExtension` / `EnableSyncOverAsync()`). **In .NET 11 (EF Core 11), that opt-in is removed entirely.** Synchronous LINQ operators against the Cosmos provider now always throw `InvalidOperationException`.

**All four methods break:**

| Method | Sync call that throws |
|---|---|
| `GetAll()` | `ToList()` |
| `GetById()` | `First()` |
| `GetCount()` | `Count()` |
| `Save()` | `SaveChanges()` |

## Fix: convert to async

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `Add()` is an in-memory operation — it stays synchronous. Only the I/O call (`SaveChangesAsync`) needs the change.
- All callers up the chain must propagate `async/await` (controllers, services, etc.).
- There is no workaround — the Cosmos provider is now **async-only** for all query and save operations that hit the network.
